course: dictionary
lesson: 7875
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them, the context, tell you which meaning the writer wants. Raj starts with a capital letter here, and the sentences around it give more clues.
explain: «He spends more time with Raj, who never asks for anything and always brings two biscuits.» Here Raj is a friend. Nobody rules a friend, so the rule meaning does not fit. Raj is a person's name.
explain: In history lessons, the Raj means the time when Britain ruled India. Raj is also a Hindi word meaning rule or kingdom. To check, swap your meaning into the sentence. If «rule» does not fit, you have chosen the wrong meaning.
fact: Raj is a common boy's name in India and among Indian families.
fact: The Raj, or British Raj, was the time when Britain ruled India.
fact: Raj is a Hindi word meaning rule or kingdom.
fact: Words from the time of British rule came into English, such as bungalow, shampoo, pyjamas and jungle.
fact: A word with several meanings is called a homonym or a multiple-meaning word; the context tells you which one to use.
exercise: «Connor met Raj at football: both were rubbish, both got stuck in defence.» What is Raj here? | A football team | *A boy's name | A kind of biscuit | The time when Britain ruled India
exercise: In a history lesson, the teacher says, «The Raj ended when India became independent.» What does the Raj mean? | A school rule for pupils | A football match | *The time when Britain ruled India | A type of Indian food
exercise: «Raj rage-quits FIFA when he's losing 5–0.» What does rage-quit mean? | *Leaves the game in a temper | Asks for a rematch | Wins the game with a big score | Plays the game very slowly
test: Raj is a Hindi word. What does it mean? | A temper | A biscuit | *Rule or kingdom | A football
test: «Words from that time came into English: bungalow, shampoo, pyjamas, jungle.» Which of these came into English from the time of the Raj? | Football | Biscuit | *Shampoo | Minecraft
exam: Which clue in «Connor met Raj at football» shows that Raj is a person's name? | He is a kind of rule | He is a biscuit | He is a country ruled by Britain | *He is a person who played football with Connor
